It's very late in the game... and just below the castle you have the
mazes...

Almost all of the equipment you need is all done and set, and
everything is mostly set. Every level is the same... nothing
different, bunches of items, tons of gold, but it isn't really worth
searching through. I mean like... you have the demon layers, which can
be okay, but you just have mazes mazes and mazes...

After thinking lots about it... what makes nethack unique is that
everything is created randomly, and you get lots of variety in what
sort of levels you bump into, little temples, beehives, etc~ but as
soon as you hit Gehommen *poof* bunches of mazes, pre-set levels, and
nothing else.

Shouldn't there be difficult things in gehommen aside from demons? No
little random castles? No little pools or troubles? No nasty ways you
could die aside from a silly mistake?

Random types of mazes have been tried... we have the heck patch, which
is going nicely despite not really being developed... but... what
could be done to make Gehommen more nethackish? It's too mazey...
occasional mazes are nice, but having half the dungeon be them is
kinda tedius... if I'm trying to find Vlad's I'd rather not dig out
the same level a dozen times... I'm tired and babbling, it's so fun...
maybe I'll ascend again soon, I always seem to do that after losing my
"best characters" ....

